# Rust build output
/target
**/target

# Node / napi
node_modules/
*.node
dist-node/
crates/zero-migrate-node/package-lock.json
# NOTE: pnpm-lock.yaml is intentionally TRACKED (not ignored) so CI's
# `actions/setup-node` pnpm cache + `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` work.

# Derived TS build output (tsup/tsc). Everything under dist/ is regenerated by
# `pnpm build` and ignored, except embedded-recorder.js, which is tracked because
# the package test script runs without a build: tests/ops.test.ts,
# tests/column-facets-lockstep.test.ts and tests/sequences-exclusion.test.ts
# import it directly, so a fresh checkout has a bundle to import. CI builds first
# and then gates the committed copy against the rebuild.
#
# No Rust code reads this file. Nothing under crates/ names it, and the recorder
# the engine talks to is the JS one that hands ops across the N-API bridge, not
# this bundle.
packages/*/dist/
!packages/zero-migrate/dist/
packages/zero-migrate/dist/*
!packages/zero-migrate/dist/embedded-recorder.js

# napi build artifacts. The generated `index.js` (platform-resolving loader) and
# `index.d.ts` (the typed ABI surface, the single source of truth the engine's
# addon.ts imports) ARE tracked: they let any checkout typecheck/build without a
# Rust toolchain, and are the published entry of the `zero-migrate-node` package.
# Only the compiled `.node` binaries are per-platform build output.
crates/zero-migrate-node/*.node
# The per-platform npm/<triple>/ dirs are regenerated at release time by
# `napi create-npm-dirs`; do not track them.
crates/zero-migrate-node/npm/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp

# A local dev stub that satisfies a `file:` link in some working copies. It calls
# itself `zero-migrate` at version `0.0.0-stub`, so tracking it would put a second
# thing claiming that package name in the tree. Two commits have now swept it in by
# accident via `git add -A`; ignoring it is what stops a third. Whether such a stub
# should exist at all is a separate open question and this entry does not answer it.
sdks/

# Working notes for the review loop. Deliberately never committed.
docs/review-log/
